     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:150%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Dear Karl<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:150%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">I have scaned QTLs in two chromosomes using MQM. I am not sure if I am\r\ncorrect undersanding the results. I have obtained high LOD score values using\r\nmqmscan. The problem is that when I run the function including cofactors\r\n(mqmautocofactors), the output shows low LODs. <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:150%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:150%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">mqm&lt;-mqmscan(misdatosaug, cofactors=NULL,pheno.col=2,\r\nmodel=c(&quot;additive&quot;,&quot;dominance&quot;), forceML=F, em.iter=1000,\r\nwindow.size=10, step.size=5) <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:150%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">autocofactors &lt;- mqmautocofactor